From eb7eba14f104ee2a0f1c3e9c0c411d082aa42886 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Wikman <lars@underjord.io>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:39:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] spi: qup: don't leak a clock enable on resume while runtime
 suspended

spi_qup_suspend() runtime resumes a runtime suspended controller so it
can reset it, then disables the clocks. spi_qup_resume() always enables
them again, but the device is still runtime suspended, so nothing
disables them: each system suspend taken while the bus is idle leaves
the core and iface clocks enabled once more.

Put a controller that was runtime suspended back into that state at the
end of resume.

Signed-off-by: Lars Wikman <lars@underjord.io>
---
 drivers/spi/spi-qup.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-qup.c b/drivers/spi/spi-qup.c
index 0ca97ae..087b03f 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-qup.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-qup.c
@@ -1309,6 +1309,13 @@ static int spi_qup_resume(struct device *device)
 	if (ret)
 		goto disable_clk;
 
+	/*
+	 * A controller that was runtime suspended stays so: its runtime resume
+	 * will enable the clocks again.
+	 */
+	if (pm_runtime_suspended(device))
+		return spi_qup_pm_suspend_runtime(device);
+
 	return 0;
 
 disable_clk:
-- 
2.43.0

